package hartland.worlds
model world

// AU (automation agents) — the hartland demo world: where the recipes of `automation/` (P2 on) read and
// write. contracts.md §3 (project/kantheon/features/automation-agents/implementation/hartland/); the qname
// `hartland.worlds.demo` is what a recipe names in `uses world "hartland.worlds.demo"` (17 §3).
//
// ONE WORLD FILE, TWO WORLDS BY CONNECTION. Hartland is one model over two databases (US `hartland_us`,
// CZ `hartland_cz`), and the world follows: nothing here names a world's database. A bundle reads its
// credentials from `TTR_CONN_<ENGINE>` (ttr-p contracts §5; the engine name upper-cased), so
//   TTR_CONN_ERP        → `hartland_us` or `hartland_cz`,
//   TTR_CONN_AUTOMATION → the `automation` database, search_path `us` or `cz` (⚑AU-P-2 = D-118),
// and the deployment that sets them picks the world. The CZ recipes differ from the US ones only in prose.
//
// Written in the pinned toolchain's `model world` grammar (ttr-core grammar 0.15.1: `def world` holding
// `def engine` / `def storage`; staging is a storage flag). contracts §3 sketched the ttr-core P0 shape
// (`schema world`, `writable:`, `connection:`); what 0.15.1 has no typed property for is a comment below,
// not invented syntax:
//   - `writable:` (D-76, D-79) — ttr-core P0. The writer's targets are a contract; the suite holds them
//     as a `test.todo` (model/tests/automation-extension.test.mjs) until the property exists;
//   - `connection:` — not needed: the engine's name IS the credential name (above);
//   - `schemas: [dbo]`, `rls: true` — the ERP's model-mapped schema and its row-level rules (LR G2) — P2
//     re-reads them against the toolchain then pinned.
// The identities, executors, grants, deployments and the `def process` of 17 §2 land with them at P2.

def world demo {
    description: "Hartland demo world — the ERP (the hartland warehouse, one per world) and the automation ledger."

    def engine erp        { type: postgres }
    def engine automation { type: postgres }

    // writable: [order.state, order.held_for, return_request_line.state, return_request_line.way,
    //            reorder_proposal, winback_mail]                                        — D-79, ttr-core P0
    // schemas: [dbo], rls: true                                                         — P2
    def storage erp_db { type: postgres, via: erp, hosts: [hartland] }

    // writable: [obligation, state_history, "*_verdict", "*_verdict_detail", approvals] — D-76, ttr-core P0
    def storage automation_db { type: postgres, via: automation }

    // Island outputs of a run land here as Arrow IPC, `runs/{id}/{island}.{port}.arrow` (10 B-6); the
    // automation service roots the directory and releases it at close + grace (D-73).
    def storage stage { type: local_dir, staging: true }
}
